# Chore validation
### Weekly rule without weekdays, should return 400

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/new-chore
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Invalid chore",
  "frequency": 1,
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-10T00:00:00+01:00"
}

### Weekdays on a monthly rule, should return 400

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/new-chore
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Invalid chore",
  "frequency": 2,
  "weekdays": 1,
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-10T00:00:00+01:00"
}

### Interval of 0, should return 400

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/new-chore
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Invalid chore",
  "frequency": 0,
  "interval": 0,
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-10T00:00:00+01:00"
}

### Weekdays without frequency, should return 400

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/new-chore
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Invalid chore",
  "weekdays": 1,
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-10T00:00:00+01:00"
}

# Chore and ChoreInstance
### Creates a one-off chore without a rule, gets chore 1 and instance 1

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/new-chore
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mop the floors",
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-10T00:00:00+01:00"
}

### Vacuum every Monday and Thursday (9), chore 2. The instance on 12 Nov is created by hand, the rest is generated up to 4 weeks ahead

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/new-chore
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Vacuum",
  "frequency": 1,
  "weekdays": 9,
  "startDate": "2026-11-09",
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-12T00:00:00+01:00"
}

### Change the sheets every second Sunday (64), chore 3. Should give 15 Nov and 29 Nov

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/new-chore
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Change the sheets",
  "frequency": 1,
  "interval": 2,
  "weekdays": 64,
  "startDate": "2026-11-15",
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-15T00:00:00+01:00"
}

### Pay the rent on the 31st every month, chore 4. November has 30 days, so it falls on 30 Nov

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/new-chore
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Pay the rent",
  "frequency": 2,
  "startDate": "2026-10-31",
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-30T00:00:00+01:00"
}

### Gets all chores for household 1

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Gets chore 2

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Gets chore 999, should return 404

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Gets all instances for household 1

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Gets the instances for the week 9 Nov to 16 Nov (to is not included). Note that + in the time zone must be written as %2B

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances?from=2026-11-09T00:00:00%2B01:00&to=2026-11-16T00:00:00%2B01:00
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Gets instance 2

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Instance for a chore that doesn't exist, should return 404

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "choreId": 999,
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-10T00:00:00+01:00"
}

### Creates an extra instance for chore 1

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "choreId": 1,
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-11T00:00:00+01:00"
}

### Marks instance 1 as done

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/1/mark-as-done
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Clears the done date on instance 1

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/1/clear-done-date
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Skips instance 3 (Vacuum on 16 Nov). It stays in the list with isSkipped true and is not generated again

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/3/mark-as-skipped
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Skips instance 4 and then clears it again

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/4/mark-as-skipped
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/4/clear-skipped-date
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Marks the skipped instance 3 as done, which clears the skip

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/3/mark-as-done
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Skips instance 3 again, which clears the done date

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/3/mark-as-skipped
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Updates the name on chore 4

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/4
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Pay the rent on time"
}

### Assigns chore 2 to the child

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{childId}}"
}

### Only the chores for the child, should be chore 2

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores?userId={{childId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Only the instances for the child, should be the instances for chore 2

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances?userId={{childId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Adds a rule to chore 1 without startDate, should return 400

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "frequency": 0
}

### Chore 3 becomes weekly on Sundays (64) every week. Open instances from today are generated again after the new rule

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/3
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "frequency": 1,
  "interval": 1,
  "weekdays": 64,
  "startDate": "2026-11-15"
}

### Instances for chore 3 are now every Sunday, should be 15, 22 and 29 Nov and 6 Dec

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances?from=2026-11-14T00:00:00%2B01:00&to=2026-12-08T00:00:00%2B01:00
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Weekdays on a daily rule, should return 400

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/3
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "frequency": 0,
  "weekdays": 1
}

### Renames chore 2 for the future, should return a NEW chore 5 with a new id and the same rule. Open instances from tomorrow move over to it, the skipped one stays on chore 2

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/2/update-future
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Vacuum everything"
}

### Chore 2 has only the skipped instance left, chore 5 has the rest and does not get 16 Nov

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances?from=2026-11-09T00:00:00%2B01:00&to=2026-12-08T00:00:00%2B01:00
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Nothing changed, should return chore 5 itself (same id, no new chore created)

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/5/update-future
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Vacuum everything"
}

### Chore without a rule (chore 1), should return 404

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/1/update-future
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Whatever"
}

### Deletes one instance of the recurring chore 5. The chore stays. It is created again by the nightly generation, so skipping is the right way to leave one out

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/18
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Deletes both instances of the one-off chore 1, the chore is removed with the last one

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/13
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Chore 1 is gone, should return 404

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# Images
### Uploads an image for recipe 1

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Recipes/1/image
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----HouseholdBoundary

------HouseholdBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./HttpSamples/sample.png
------HouseholdBoundary--

### Gets the image for recipe 1, should return image/png

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Recipes/1/image
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Recipe 1 should now have hasImage true

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Recipes/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A text file named .png, should return 400 because the content is checked

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Recipes/1/image
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----HouseholdBoundary

------HouseholdBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="not-an-image.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./HttpSamples/not-an-image.png
------HouseholdBoundary--

### A PDF as recipe image, should return 400

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Recipes/1/image
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----HouseholdBoundary

------HouseholdBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./HttpSamples/sample.pdf
------HouseholdBoundary--

### Image for a recipe that doesn't exist, should return 404

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Recipes/999/image
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----HouseholdBoundary

------HouseholdBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./HttpSamples/sample.png
------HouseholdBoundary--

### Removes the image from recipe 1

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/Recipes/1/image
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The image is gone, should return 404

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Recipes/1/image
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# SchoolPlan
### Uploads a school plan for the week of 9 Nov (any date in the week is moved to the Monday), gets id 1

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/SchoolPlans
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----HouseholdBoundary

------HouseholdBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="weekDate"

2026-11-12
------HouseholdBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./HttpSamples/sample.pdf
------HouseholdBoundary--

### Uploads an image as a school plan for the same week, gets id 2

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/SchoolPlans
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----HouseholdBoundary

------HouseholdBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="weekDate"

2026-11-09
------HouseholdBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./HttpSamples/sample.png
------HouseholdBoundary--

### A text file, should return 400

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/SchoolPlans
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----HouseholdBoundary

------HouseholdBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="weekDate"

2026-11-09
------HouseholdBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="not-an-image.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./HttpSamples/not-an-image.png
------HouseholdBoundary--

### Gets all school plans for household 1

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/SchoolPlans
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Gets the school plans for the week containing 11 Nov

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/SchoolPlans?weekDate=2026-11-11
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Gets the school plans for another week, should be empty

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/SchoolPlans?weekDate=2026-11-18
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Gets school plan 1

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/SchoolPlans/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Gets the file for school plan 1, should return application/pdf

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/SchoolPlans/1/file
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Deletes school plan 2

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/SchoolPlans/2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### School plan 2 is gone, should return 404

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/SchoolPlans/2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# Ending and deleting chores
### Creates a daily chore, gets a new chore id and daily instances
# @name dailyChore
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances/new-chore
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Water the plants",
  "frequency": 0,
  "startDate": "2026-11-10",
  "periodStartDate": "2026-11-10T00:00:00+01:00"
}

### Ends the recurrence from tomorrow, the chore stays without a rule and open instances from tomorrow are removed. Replace 6 with the chore id from the response above

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/6/end
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Deletes the chore with all its instances

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores/6
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Only open instances up to a date, use it to find overdue chores

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances?to=2026-11-10T00:00:00%2B01:00&onlyOpen=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# Shopping list cleanup
### Clears all bought items, returns deletedCount

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/ShoppingItems/bought
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# Passwords and tokens
### Changes the password of the logged in user, returns a new token pair and invalidates the old refresh tokens

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{childToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "{{childPassword}}",
  "newPassword": "{{childPassword}}x"
}

### The old password no longer works, should return 401

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "{{childUserName}}",
  "password": "{{childPassword}}"
}

### The admin resets the password of the child back to the original

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/{{childId}}/reset-password
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newPassword": "{{childPassword}}"
}

### Logs in as the child again and refreshes. Paste the refreshToken from the response into refreshTokenValue below
# @name childLogin2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "{{childUserName}}",
  "password": "{{childPassword}}"
}

###
@refreshTokenValue = {{childLogin2.response.body.$.refreshToken}}

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshTokenValue}}"
}

### The same refresh token used again, should return 401 and revoke all tokens for the child

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshTokenValue}}"
}

### Logout with a token that is already revoked, should return 204

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshTokenValue}}"
}

# Users
### Lists the users of the household with role and isActive

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Gets the child

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/{{childId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A user id that does not exist, should return 404

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/does-not-exist
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Who am I, as the admin

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Who am I, as the child

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{childToken}}

### Deactivates the child, isActive becomes false and the child can no longer log in (should return 429)

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/{{childId}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "{{childUserName}}",
  "password": "{{childPassword}}"
}

### Activates the child again

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/{{childId}}/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Creates a throwaway user that is deleted below
# @name throwaway
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "Throwaway",
  "password": "Throwaway12345!",
  "role": "child"
}

### Deletes the throwaway user, should return 204

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/{{throwaway.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The throwaway user is gone, should return 404

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/{{throwaway.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The admin cannot delete itself, should return 400 (the admin id comes from /me)
# @name me
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/{{me.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The child cannot list users, should return 403

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Users
Authorization: Bearer {{childToken}}

# The child
### The child sees only its own chores

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Chores
Authorization: Bearer {{childToken}}

### The child sees only its own instances

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ChoreInstances
Authorization: Bearer {{childToken}}

### The child can see recipes and school plans

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Recipes
Authorization: Bearer {{childToken}}

###

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/SchoolPlans
Authorization: Bearer {{childToken}}

### The child can add to the shopping list

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ShoppingItems
Authorization: Bearer {{childToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "amount": 1,
  "unit": 5
}

### The child can not create recipes, should return 403

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Recipes
Authorization: Bearer {{childToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Not allowed"
}

### The child can not delete shopping items, should return 403

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/ShoppingItems/1
Authorization: Bearer {{childToken}}

### The child can not create users, should return 403

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Users
Authorization: Bearer {{childToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "Another",
  "password": "Another12345!",
  "role": "child"
}

### The admin cannot delete its own household, should return 400

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/Households/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# Lockout, run this last because it locks the child out for 15 minutes
### Five wrong passwords lock the account, the sixth attempt should return 429 even with the correct password

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "{{childUserName}}",
  "password": "wrong"
}
